{title: Auld Lang Syne}
{artist: Robert Burns, 1788}
{key: D}
{tempo: 80}
{difficulty: intermediate}
{tags: folk, scottish, holiday}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Should auld ac[D]quaintance be for[A]got
And [D]never [D7]brought to [G]mind?
Should auld ac[D]quaintance be for[A]got
And [Bm]auld [G]lang [A]syne[D]

{start_of_chorus}
For [D]auld lang syne, my [A]dear
For [D]auld [D7]lang [G]syne
We'll take a [D]cup o' kindness [A]yet
For [Bm]auld [G]lang [A]syne[D]

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
And surely [D]ye'll be your pint-[A]stowp
And [D]surely [D7]I'll be [G]mine
And we'll take a [D]cup o' kindness [A]yet
For [Bm]auld [G]lang [A]syne[D]

{chorus}
